{"title":"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_-_Trial_and_Error\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 - Trial and Error</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(not_rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (not rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6e1ebffbc1cb0eec51440bbe0ddd5c03ba6b5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" /> are written in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d7104f34af16053b63ce7cfa87265d915c6105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> array of squares, one number in each square, in such a way that if two numbers are consecutive then they occupy squares that share an edge. The numbers in the four corners add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. What is the number in the center?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97af68b0e27ddcc9bb656fba006759ed49696f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consecutive numbers share an edge. That means that it is possible to walk from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by single steps north, south, east, or west. Consequently, the squares in the diagram with different shades have different parity:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f39f0e7b752d26dd1dc58cc402af636029b64af9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(4cm); for(int i=0;i&lt;3;++i)for(int j=0;j&lt;3;++j)filldraw(box((i,j),(i+1,j+1)),gray((i+j)%2*.2+.7));[/asy]\" width=\"192\" height=\"192\" />\nBut since there are only four even numbers in the set, the five darker squares must contain the odd numbers, which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96290ff849fc7a1335ca7e6ca3f51c880f3c694.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+3+5+7+9=25.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"180\" height=\"14\" /> Therefore if the sum of the numbers in the corners is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the number in the center must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e28dcbdcd6be4be02beb725aa6dd025ac87f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_-_Trial_and_Error\">Solution 2 - Trial and Error</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 - Trial and Error\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Quick testing shows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/5/3a51c280f2c1f293c56ef5ade79e8cf929032f16.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3~2~1\\]\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b451d8e5438bb977e84409ebde060296f919f95e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4~7~8\\]\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a0e6b99a06bf9a2eda08c3fd65ec5e6073ddc0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5~6~9\\]\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" />\nis a valid solution. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/c/8fcfa4a623c3b03e912ea2e0c124dad66c3a77a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+1+5+9 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />, and the numbers follow the given condition. The center number is found to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e28dcbdcd6be4be02beb725aa6dd025ac87f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />.. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Adihaya\" title=\"User:Adihaya\">— @adihaya</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User_talk:Adihaya\" title=\"User talk:Adihaya\">talk</a>) 12:27, 21 February 2016 (EST) ~edited\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28not_rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(not_rigorous)\">Solution 3 (not rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (not rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First let the numbers be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bcdb07a2e0f1753b2fcff3951d784fbc30eb50b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1   ~8~   7\\]\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e97fdf3f74cf5c7dc9362dfe41d551990a03eb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2  ~ 9   ~6\\]\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb90e4cb8f0fe8760958e2b5678f6d84044007dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3  ~ 4~   5\\]\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />\nwith the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eed1fe1051319d0a323e860bcf49a150c264e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> around the outsides and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the middle. We see that the sum of the four corner numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If we switch <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the corner numbers will add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the consecutive numbers will still be touching each other. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e28dcbdcd6be4be02beb725aa6dd025ac87f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />. ~edited\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(answer_choices)\">Solution 4 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Testing out the box with the center square taking on the value of 5 and 6, we find that they either do not satisfy the first or the second condition. Testing 7, we find that a valid configuration is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b3004c9d8193debf2b2a5c48bdb4ae0f6ea527b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 ~8~ 9\\]\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0b346fc28c358ea8959b215cb918b953fb1502.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 ~ 7 ~6\\]\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb90e4cb8f0fe8760958e2b5678f6d84044007dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3 ~ 4~ 5\\]\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e28dcbdcd6be4be02beb725aa6dd025ac87f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~JH. L\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3856d888046107ef12e2b33c2065737e0b2602d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> adding to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Like Solution 1, you realize that all the dark squares are all odd numbers, and the only case with all odd numbers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/6/0a6444db71573397faed8b4235119729ca9acc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,5,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />, meaning that the center square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/e/a8e28dcbdcd6be4be02beb725aa6dd025ac87f6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(C) }7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"57\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B\">2016 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2016 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153021\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 279/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6049/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.280      1 -total\n 54.92%    7.843      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 44.09%    6.296      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14799:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153021 and revision id 271192. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}